@startuml graph-update
title US-05: Graph Update - Proximity Event Written to Neo4j; candidate published for unscheduled pairs

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Correlation
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka

Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE Entity nodes for both entities\n(creates if absent, matches if present)

note over Correlation
  pair_key = min(entity_a_id, entity_b_id) + ':' + max(entity_a_id, entity_b_id)
  episode_start_ms = position event's timestamp_ms (source event time)
  idempotency_key = {pair_key}:{episode_start_ms}
  One edge per proximity episode.
end note

Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge\nidempotency_key = {idempotency_key}\nON CREATE: set episode_start_ms, distance_at_detection, lat, lon\nON MATCH: update last_seen_ms, min_distance_metres if closer

note over Neo4j
  Idempotency key = {pair_key}:{episode_start_ms}.
  Replaying the same Kafka event matches the existing edge — no duplicate.
  ON MATCH updates keep last_seen_ms and min_distance_metres
  current during an ongoing episode.
  Safe to replay from any offset.
end note

Neo4j --> Correlation : edge created or updated

note over Correlation
  Neo4j write applies to ALL close pairs
  (unscheduled and known associates).
  Kafka publish below applies to unscheduled pairs only.
end note

Correlation -> ProxKafka : publish proximity.candidates\n(unscheduled pairs only)\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, lat, lon, distance_at_detection }

note over ProxKafka
  Published only on episode start — not on each ping.
  Published only when no KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge exists.
  Known associates: Neo4j edge written, no Kafka event.
  Alert Evaluator consumes this topic to emit
  UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY and COMPOSITE alerts.
  Short retention (1h) — stale candidates have no value.
end note

@enduml
